model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Node usage and application diagnostics retain only bounded metadata while preserving Home selection identity and request outcomes. Credentials, payload bodies, token fingerprints and arbitrary error text never enter metadata-only diagnostics. The carry preserves upstream authentication policy fields and their refresh behavior independently of diagnostic redaction, including version-specific request-scoped error rules. Model provider stream redaction guards model retention without changing the upstream model-update condition or token accounting. Every configuration the node loads applies metadata-only diagnostics, including the store-backed standby configuration. In metadata-only mode the queued usage record omits the account identifier and plugin-attributed source, and an attempt model replaces the admitted usage model only when it is a registered model."
    }
  }
}
